    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A man bought a house and had some renovations done. The renovations cost $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the price of the house. He paid $\\$980\\,000$ for the house and the renovations. What was the price of the house?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$840\\,000$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ dollars be the price of the house. The renovations cost $\\frac{x}{6}$ dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{x}{6}&=980\\,000\\\\6x+x&=5\\,880\\,000\\\\7x&=5\\,880\\,000\\\\x&=840\\,000\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe price of the house was $\\$840\\,000$.",
